# React Native Performance

Default to "production-ready mobile architecture", not "works on my phone".

## Bridge & threading

- Minimize bridge calls. Batch native calls; never poll across the bridge in
  a `setInterval`. Move repeated work to native modules or Reanimated worklets.
- Never block the JS thread. Anything > 16ms gets deferred via
  `InteractionManager.runAfterInteractions`, a worklet, or a native module.
- Split heavy business logic out of the UI thread (worklets, JSI modules,
  background tasks) — UI thread is for layout + paint only.

## Animations

- Prefer native-driven animations: Reanimated worklets, or RN `Animated` with
  `useNativeDriver: true`. JS-driven animations on low-end Android = jank.
- Avoid layout thrashing — don't `measure()` and `setState()` in the same
  frame. Move dynamic measurements to `onLayout` or worklets.
- Gesture handling goes through `react-native-gesture-handler` (runs on UI
  thread), never raw `PanResponder`.

## Re-renders (low-end Android)

- Profile against a low-RAM Android device (≤ 2GB) — what's smooth on iPhone
  Pro will stutter on a Pixel 3a. Enable Perf Monitor (`⌘D` → Perf Monitor)
  and aim for 60 FPS JS / 60 FPS UI.
- Memoize `renderItem` and any callback props that go into memoized children.
  Inline arrow functions = new reference every render = forced child re-render.
- Avoid unstable references in props — `style={{...}}`, `data={[...]}`, and
  inline objects break shallow equality.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — new array & new fn every parent render
<FlatList data={[...items]} renderItem={(x) => <Row item={x.item} />} />

// ✅ GOOD — stable references
const renderItem = useCallback(({ item }) => <Row item={item} />, []);
<FlatList data={items} renderItem={renderItem} keyExtractor={keyExtractor} />
```

## Bundle & startup

- Optimize startup time — measure `TTI` (time to interactive) on a cold start.
  Defer non-critical imports (`require()` lazily inside handlers).
- Lazy-load heavy screens via Expo Router's file-based code-splitting; don't
  eager-import giant deps (charting, video, ML kits) in `_layout.tsx`.
- Compress images aggressively. Use WebP, ship `@1x` / `@2x` / `@3x` only as
  needed, prefer `expo-image` (caches + native decode).
- Audit JS bundle size — `npx expo export` then inspect `_expo/static/js/*.hbc`.
  Drop the largest 3 deps you don't need.
- Profile under Hermes (it's the default). Use Hermes' sampling profiler when
  a screen feels slow.
